1
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:17,919
Here.

2
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:18,960
Give it to me.

3
00:02:46,039 --> 00:02:47,800
Isn't this highway newly built?

4
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:48,639
What about the cameras?

5
00:02:48,639 --> 00:02:49,960
They aren't fully installed yet.

6
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,000
So tracking them is extremely difficult.

7
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,280
I called him, but he didn't answer.

8
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:08,960
It's been nine years.

9
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,520
I could never understand

10
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:14,840
why heaven would play such a trick on me.

11
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,800
But I just realized

12
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:20,599
I just hadn't seen the big picture.

13
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,879
Now, heaven has given me a gift.

14
00:03:26,199 --> 00:03:27,000
So,

15
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,400
thank you very much,

16
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:36,159
Zhao Yijie.

17
00:03:36,919 --> 00:03:39,479
You're the one who brought me new hope.

18
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:43,039
A chance to truly protect my family.

19
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,840
I will truly cherish this opportunity.

20
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:50,280
You always thought adopting Yang A'wu

21
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,960
you could trap and use me.

22
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,000
But did you ever consider

23
00:03:55,319 --> 00:03:57,120
that I could actually use you too?

24
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:00,080
Use you to do things that must be done,

25
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,560
but that I can't bring myself to do.

26
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:04,039
What are you writing?

27
00:04:06,599 --> 00:04:07,240
Nothing.

28
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:09,800
Don't worry. Go back to your work.

29
00:04:21,759 --> 00:04:22,319
Grandpa!

30
00:04:23,439 --> 00:04:24,160
This way.

31
00:04:25,079 --> 00:04:25,920
That way?

32
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,079
What is it?

33
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:30,079
Piggyback.

34
00:04:30,199 --> 00:04:30,839
A piggyback?

35
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:33,680
Come on then.

36
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:37,199
Up we go.

37
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,600
Here we go!

38
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:43,079
Oh no, A'wu needs to pee.

39
00:04:43,519 --> 00:04:45,720
What? You need to pee?

40
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,279
Alright, then pee right here, okay?

41
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:48,920
Fooled you, Grandpa!

42
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,360
You fooled me?

43
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:52,800
You fooled me! You little trickster!

44
00:04:53,439 --> 00:04:54,240
So impressive!

45
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:54,839
Grandpa!

46
00:04:54,839 --> 00:04:55,600
What is it?

47
00:04:55,839 --> 00:04:57,319
A'wu wants ice cream.

48
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:58,879
Ice cream?

49
00:04:59,879 --> 00:05:02,759
Didn't you eat a bunch of popsicles today?

50
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,920
If you eat more, you'll get a tummy ache.

51
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:05,920
And do stinky poops.

52
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,839
I want it anyway!

53
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,319
Or else I'll poop on Grandpa's neck!

54
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:11,600
Really?

55
00:05:12,079 --> 00:05:13,120
Are you sure?

56
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:15,720
You're gonna poop on my neck? Are you?

57
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,839
Then how about I let you poop on my neck?

58
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,120
Here, can you poop upside down?

59
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,360
Can you poop like this?

60
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,240
Grandpa!

61
00:06:03,319 --> 00:06:04,079
Manghao Man!

62
00:06:04,079 --> 00:06:05,199
Look, it's the Manghao Man!

63
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:50,480
I've already lost my wife,

64
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,199
lost my son.

65
00:06:53,279 --> 00:06:53,600
Now,

66
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,800
even my lifelong faith in the law

67
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:56,800
is gone.

68
00:07:00,519 --> 00:07:01,920
A'wu is all I have left.

69
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,000
What is this?

70
00:07:12,959 --> 00:07:13,800
A peacock.

71
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,319
Right.

72
00:07:14,839 --> 00:07:15,920
A peacock.

73
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,959
What does a peacock do?

74
00:07:18,199 --> 00:07:19,759
A peacock goes to court!

75
00:07:19,879 --> 00:07:22,000
A peacock spreads its tail.

76
00:07:22,399 --> 00:07:24,560
Grandpa is the one who goes to court!

77
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,079
Come on.

78
00:07:40,319 --> 00:07:43,279
Let's have some water and go to sleep.

79
00:07:43,519 --> 00:07:44,120
Here.

80
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:46,680
Have some water and then sleep, okay?

81
00:07:48,839 --> 00:07:49,560
Ding Ning.

82
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,240
Ding Ning.

83
00:07:51,319 --> 00:07:52,240
She'll come.

84
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,800
Ding Ning isn't coming.

85
00:07:58,519 --> 00:07:59,519
She has to work.

86
00:08:01,879 --> 00:08:03,160
Zhao Yijie.

87
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:08,519
Zhao Yijie isn't coming either.

88
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:10,079
He has to work too.

89
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:14,879
It's just the two of us.

90
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:17,240
Nobody else is coming.

91
00:08:17,439 --> 00:08:19,120
We're going on a trip.

92
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:19,959
You know?

93
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,879
We'll go to lots and lots of places.

94
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:29,720
And watch the sun rise and set everywhere.

95
00:08:30,439 --> 00:08:32,799
We can also look at the white clouds,

96
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,039
and have some delicious...

97
00:08:35,919 --> 00:08:38,159
cotton candy that looks like white clouds.

98
00:08:53,159 --> 00:08:55,440
Don't you want just the two of us?

99
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:15,879
Yu Songfan sent another letter.

100
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:17,600
Read it.

101
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,679
Greetings, Zhao Yijie.

102
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,840
A'wu and I saw the bauhinia flowers today.

103
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,159
By the way,

104
00:09:32,559 --> 00:09:34,759
A'wu ate 18 dumplings last night.

105
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,120
That's 18 of them.

106
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,399
I forgot.

107
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,279
He's not even your son.

108
00:09:40,279 --> 00:09:41,960
Why would you care about that?

109
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,840
Let's get to the point.

110
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:46,440
You love sending me math tests, don't you?

111
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:49,200
Then I guess a good student like you

112
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,360
must also enjoy literature tests, right?

113
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:54,200
So how about I give you a question?

114
00:09:55,559 --> 00:09:57,120
Before that, I forgot to mention...

115
00:09:57,559 --> 00:09:58,879
You're not the only one who looked into me.

116
00:09:59,159 --> 00:10:01,200
Before taking A'wu away, I also

117
00:10:01,399 --> 00:10:03,600
used all my judicial connections

118
00:10:03,639 --> 00:10:05,519
to dig into your background.

119
00:10:06,159 --> 00:10:08,200
I'm guessing you and your backers

120
00:10:09,039 --> 00:10:10,200
have already been targeted.

121
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:13,200
You should know this without me saying it.

122
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:16,200
You've been close to Fuxia Group lately.

123
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,639
Fuxia Group is being investigated.

124
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,000
How far along is the investigation now?

125
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,240
He's the kind of guy

126
00:10:34,279 --> 00:10:35,480
who always takes the hard path.

127
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,080
Our biggest breakthrough so far

128
00:10:38,559 --> 00:10:39,919
is that next to Jiangyu Highway,

129
00:10:39,919 --> 00:10:41,600
in a supermarket trash can,

130
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:43,080
we found a phone he threw away.

131
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,159
I told you.

132
00:10:45,159 --> 00:10:46,440
I need to know where he is.

133
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,799
He's very cautious.

134
00:10:47,799 --> 00:10:48,559
We followed him the whole way,

135
00:10:48,559 --> 00:10:50,440
and he either switched cars or plates.

136
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,799
He even wore a disguise.

137
00:10:51,799 --> 00:10:53,120
He only pays in cash.

138
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:53,759
And also,

139
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:55,879
I don't know when he

140
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,399
got a fake ID.

141
00:10:57,519 --> 00:10:59,039
Don't give me all these excuses.

142
00:10:59,279 --> 00:11:01,000
Now he even knows about Fuxia Group!

143
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,279
Then go call the police yourself.

144
00:11:02,279 --> 00:11:03,559
Tell the cops.

145
00:11:05,879 --> 00:11:07,000
I've always handled your matters

146
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,399
as my own.

147
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,799
You think this is what I want to see?

148
00:11:11,799 --> 00:11:13,320
You think I'm not upset?

149
00:11:26,639 --> 00:11:27,360
Yijie.

150
00:11:31,919 --> 00:11:33,240
Let's not try to tough it out.

151
00:11:35,559 --> 00:11:36,639
How about I go with you

152
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,320
to look for that person, okay?

153
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:57,200
Mr. Bi.

154
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:00,080
Look over there.

155
00:12:01,519 --> 00:12:03,960
Five years ago, it was all dark over there.

156
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:05,759
Time really flies.

157
00:12:06,159 --> 00:12:07,200
Thirteen years ago,

158
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,919
when Jiangliu City just overcame poverty,

159
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:12,159
Fuxia Group came to build factories here.

160
00:12:12,639 --> 00:12:13,639
It solved employment issues,

161
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:15,440
boosted related industries,

162
00:12:16,039 --> 00:12:17,720
and solved government revenue problems.

163
00:12:18,639 --> 00:12:19,399
You could say

164
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,120
that Fuxia Group is our benefactor.

165
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,240
Indeed.

166
00:12:24,399 --> 00:12:25,720
The development of our city

167
00:12:25,879 --> 00:12:27,320
truly couldn't happen without Fuxia Group.

168
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,559
But now,

169
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:30,720
times have changed.

170
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,720
Because of environmental issues,

171
00:12:32,919 --> 00:12:34,440
it has become a thorn in everyone's side.

172
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:37,080
Now, Ma Tingting's investigation team

173
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,679
won't let Fuxia Group off the hook.

174
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:41,120
I heard Ma Tingting and Yu Songfan

175
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,480
have a close mentor-mentee relationship.

176
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:43,759
Right.

177
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:46,080
Make good use of this relationship.

178
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:47,919
Alright.

179
00:12:48,759 --> 00:12:50,480
I'll handle finding Yu Songfan.

180
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:53,639
Sorry for the trouble.

181
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,600
The task of guarding this night view

182
00:12:57,759 --> 00:12:58,639
is in your hands now.

183
00:13:12,399 --> 00:13:13,039
Right.

184
00:13:13,759 --> 00:13:15,080
How are things with Ding Ning?

185
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,519
Like boiling a frog in warm water.

186
00:13:18,519 --> 00:13:21,200
I doubt she'll cause any more trouble.

187
00:13:23,919 --> 00:13:25,120
Still, we need to be careful.

188
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,879
So, regarding this issue,

189
00:13:35,879 --> 00:13:36,799
we have invited

190
00:13:36,799 --> 00:13:39,039
Lawyer Ding Ning from Rujie Law Firm.

191
00:13:39,519 --> 00:13:40,720
Now, Lawyer Ding,

192
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,679
what are your thoughts?

193
00:13:41,759 --> 00:13:44,039
If the value of these charges is huge,

194
00:13:44,279 --> 00:13:45,440
for example, if the amount involved

195
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,120
is over one or two million,

196
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,440
based on past precedents,

197
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:50,440
they'll likely face criminal liability.

198
00:13:50,679 --> 00:13:52,080
Could you give us an example?

199
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,200
Hello, Mr. Wan.

200
00:13:54,519 --> 00:13:55,200
Where are you?

201
00:13:55,519 --> 00:13:56,879
What about the recording we agreed on?

202
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:58,840
I told you yesterday afternoon.

203
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,440
I've been at Rujie for two weeks.

204
00:14:00,519 --> 00:14:02,120
Every day, you either have me shoot videos

205
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:02,960
or record programs.

206
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:04,639
I appreciate your good intentions.

207
00:14:04,799 --> 00:14:06,440
But I am a criminal defense lawyer.

208
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:07,919
I'm not a variety show star.

209
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,480
I still need to go back and take cases.

210
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,679
You were handpicked by Director Xu Ruqing,

211
00:14:11,679 --> 00:14:13,080
so I allocated all these great

212
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:13,799
promotional resources to you.

213
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:14,279
Fine.

214
00:14:14,279 --> 00:14:15,679
I'll talk to Director Xu directly, okay?

215
00:14:15,679 --> 00:14:17,120
Don't trouble yourself anymore. Thanks.

216
00:14:23,919 --> 00:14:24,639
Hello.

217
00:14:24,639 --> 00:14:26,879
Excuse me, are you a lawyer at Rujie?

218
00:14:28,159 --> 00:14:30,039
I'm a relative of a Fuxia Group employee.

219
00:14:30,039 --> 00:14:31,279
I'm a client of your firm.

220
00:14:31,279 --> 00:14:32,000
I don't have a card,

221
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:32,799
so I can't swipe in.

222
00:14:32,799 --> 00:14:34,159
I need your firm to handle a case.

223
00:14:34,159 --> 00:14:34,799
I'm sorry.

224
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,080
You need to make an appointment first.

225
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,559
Appoint... appointment? I...

226
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,080
Well,

227
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,399
who was that?

228
00:14:54,399 --> 00:14:55,159
Mrs. Lin.

229
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,000
Very clingy.

230
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,600
Don't mess with her.

231
00:14:59,679 --> 00:15:00,480
It's a D-level case.

232
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,159
Why are cases divided into levels?

233
00:15:07,279 --> 00:15:07,919
I forgot.

234
00:15:08,759 --> 00:15:09,960
You're not like us.

235
00:15:10,799 --> 00:15:11,960
You don't need to look at the system.

236
00:15:12,799 --> 00:15:14,120
You're just here to be the firm's face.

237
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:18,639
Are you still mad?

238
00:15:21,639 --> 00:15:23,159
Do I seem that petty to you?

239
00:15:27,159 --> 00:15:27,960
On a serious note,

240
00:15:29,039 --> 00:15:30,320
you and I really are different.

241
00:15:31,039 --> 00:15:32,440
You can adapt to their rules.

242
00:15:33,480 --> 00:15:34,919
So since you're at Rujie now,

243
00:15:35,279 --> 00:15:37,120
you need to make the most of it.

244
00:15:37,559 --> 00:15:38,960
Lawyer Zhao and Director Xu

245
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,480
think highly of you.

246
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,879
What a great opportunity.

247
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:44,399
Don't be like you were at Changyu Law Firm,

248
00:15:44,679 --> 00:15:46,360
focusing on those unimportant minor cases

249
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:47,159
and wasting your energy.

250
00:15:49,159 --> 00:15:50,159
It makes me anxious for you.

251
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,480
If you ask me,

252
00:15:54,159 --> 00:15:56,679
you deserve Rujie's biggest case right now.

253
00:16:00,639 --> 00:16:01,240
Morning.

254
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,840
What's the criteria for being unimportant?

255
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:07,960
Mrs. Lin's case.

256
00:16:08,279 --> 00:16:09,639
The client is her husband.

257
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,240
Her husband

258
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,320
is an ordinary programmer at Fuxia Group.

259
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:14,919
The kind that could be laid off at any time.

260
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,519
Could a case like this ever be important?

261
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,759
What's the most important case?

262
00:16:27,279 --> 00:16:28,279
Finding Liang Zidong.

263
00:16:31,639 --> 00:16:32,639
This Liang Zidong

264
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,879
is the CFO of Fuxia Group.

265
00:16:34,879 --> 00:16:36,399
An absolutely crucial figure.

266
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:37,879
He's been missing for days.

267
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,879
Likely under residential surveillance.

268
00:16:40,039 --> 00:16:40,759
And you know,

269
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,759
to take on a case like this,

270
00:16:42,759 --> 00:16:44,919
you first need to know where he's held.

271
00:16:46,039 --> 00:16:47,840
That's the most pressing matter right now.

272
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,919
But every lawyer in the firm

273
00:16:51,919 --> 00:16:52,840
is using all their tricks

274
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,000
and trying desperately to find him,

275
00:16:54,679 --> 00:16:55,879
yet there's still no clue.

276
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:58,519
His wife says she didn't receive the Designated residence surveillance notice.

277
00:16:58,519 --> 00:16:59,399
Has anyone checked?

278
00:16:59,399 --> 00:17:00,480
Is it possible

279
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,879
that his wife hid it?

280
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:03,679
Is it?

281
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,000
Why not look into that?

282
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,240
Why not investigate that connection?

283
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,799
So just because Mr. Liang is the CFO,

284
00:17:14,799 --> 00:17:16,839
and Mr. Lin is a regular programmer,

285
00:17:16,839 --> 00:17:18,839
Liang Zidong is more deserving of help?

286
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:39,079
Could you look into my husband's case?

287
00:17:39,079 --> 00:17:39,759
Please take a look.

288
00:17:39,759 --> 00:17:40,400
I'm sorry.

289
00:17:41,799 --> 00:17:43,079
Can someone help my husband?

290
00:17:43,079 --> 00:17:44,720
Please take my husband's case.

291
00:17:45,119 --> 00:17:46,240
I'm sorry, I can't.

292
00:17:46,599 --> 00:17:47,559
Please help me.

293
00:17:47,559 --> 00:17:48,119
Miss.

294
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:50,039
Could you look into my husband's case?

295
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:51,240
I can't help you, sorry.

296
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,160
I'm begging you.

297
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:53,839
Please help me.

298
00:17:53,839 --> 00:17:55,079
I'm begging you.

299
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,039
Come in.

300
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,240
Director Xu.

301
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:08,200
I want to take Mrs. Lin's case.

302
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:17,119
Even if you hadn't come to me,

303
00:18:17,119 --> 00:18:19,119
I was just about to go looking for you.

304
00:18:19,119 --> 00:18:20,960
Marketing called me several times,

305
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:21,720
saying you're

306
00:18:21,839 --> 00:18:22,640
not being very cooperative.

307
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:28,680
Here's the thing, Ding Ning.

308
00:18:29,119 --> 00:18:30,400
You see, our firm

309
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,440
has secured a lot of resources for you.

310
00:18:32,519 --> 00:18:34,200
We got you on TV shows

311
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,880
and into influencers' live streams.

312
00:18:36,119 --> 00:18:37,400
It's all to build up

313
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,799
your brand as a criminal defense lawyer.

314
00:18:39,799 --> 00:18:40,920
Well, as a criminal defense lawyer,

315
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,720
I should at least have cases to take.

316
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:44,160
But ever since I came to Rujie,

317
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,119
you guys have been so focused on packaging me

318
00:18:45,119 --> 00:18:46,640
that I haven't taken a single case.

319
00:18:47,079 --> 00:18:48,640
It's worse than when I was at Changyu.

320
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:49,960
Changyu?

321
00:18:51,119 --> 00:18:52,680
Do you think a rundown place like Changyu

322
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:54,240
could afford a star like you?

323
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,759
Ding Ning,

324
00:18:57,279 --> 00:18:58,160
you should

325
00:18:58,359 --> 00:19:00,720
trust the firm's arrangements for you.

326
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:01,799
Don't be impatient.

327
00:19:01,799 --> 00:19:03,799
We have to take it step by step, okay?

328
00:19:03,799 --> 00:19:04,640
Stop feeding me empty promises.

329
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:10,240
You need to think this through.

330
00:19:11,079 --> 00:19:13,119
As for the perks you have now,

331
00:19:13,519 --> 00:19:15,480
if it were Zhou Hao and the others,

332
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:17,480
they'd work five to eight years for them.

333
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,720
I'm not interested in shortcuts.

334
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,960
Stop beating around the bush.

335
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:22,039
I joined a law firm,

336
00:19:22,039 --> 00:19:23,680
not an influencer incubator.

337
00:19:26,279 --> 00:19:27,640
Fine. How about this?

338
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:28,640
Just wait a little longer

339
00:19:28,799 --> 00:19:30,960
until a suitable case comes along, okay?

340
00:19:31,079 --> 00:19:33,119
I want to take Mrs. Lin's case.

341
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:33,960
I'm sorry.

342
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:38,519
You can't.

343
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,000
Hello. Are you a lawyer?

344
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,200
Can you help me with a case?

345
00:19:59,200 --> 00:19:59,880
No, I can't.

346
00:20:02,759 --> 00:20:03,559
Mrs. Lin.

347
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:08,640
Hello. I'm Ding Ning from Rujie Law Firm.

348
00:20:08,759 --> 00:20:09,920
I'll take your case.

349
00:20:11,519 --> 00:20:12,240
Thank you.

350
00:20:12,599 --> 00:20:14,400
You've saved our entire family.

351
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:18,400
Let's find a place to talk.

352
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,000
Okay.

353
00:20:32,519 --> 00:20:33,160
Coming.

354
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,400
Coming, coming. Who is it?

355
00:20:42,039 --> 00:20:42,759
Son!

356
00:20:42,759 --> 00:20:43,759
Zhao Yijie.

357
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,000
Daddy's here.

358
00:20:46,799 --> 00:20:47,799
Daddy's here.

359
00:20:47,799 --> 00:20:48,839
Come here, give me a hug.

360
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:50,799
Give daddy a kiss.

361
00:20:51,519 --> 00:20:52,599
What are you doing here?

362
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:53,359
Drawing.

363
00:20:53,359 --> 00:20:54,400
Drawing, huh?

364
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:55,240
What are you drawing?

365
00:20:55,799 --> 00:20:56,480
A rainbow.

366
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:57,839
Aren't you busy lately?

367
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:00,400
Coming all this way to see us.

368
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,079
Lately,

369
00:21:02,519 --> 00:21:03,839
I've been incredibly busy.

370
00:21:06,839 --> 00:21:07,480
Here.

371
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,000
Old Yu,

372
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,480
you found a really nice place here.

373
00:21:13,839 --> 00:21:17,079
Beautiful scenery, quiet and secluded.

374
00:21:18,599 --> 00:21:19,960
Sometimes, I

375
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,559
really want to be like you

376
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,920
and run away from everything before me.

377
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:24,720
Is that so?

378
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,160
It's pretty nice here.

379
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:28,519
It really is. It's beautiful here.

380
00:21:28,599 --> 00:21:29,240
So tell me.

381
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,119
How have you been?

382
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:35,759
Are you done playing around?

383
00:21:37,079 --> 00:21:37,880
Let's go home.

384
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:40,640
We still have real business to handle.

385
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:42,279
Why should I listen to you?

386
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:46,279
Call the police, then.

387
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:50,200
I'm his real grandfather.

388
00:21:50,440 --> 00:21:51,279
Who are you?

389
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:57,279
Or maybe I should talk to the police

390
00:21:58,160 --> 00:21:59,759
about who his biological father is.

391
00:22:01,119 --> 00:22:02,799
Or I could just tell Yang A'wu directly

392
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,359
that his father is a rapist.

393
00:22:06,759 --> 00:22:09,920
Zhao Yijie, what the hell do you want?

394
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:12,440
I did what you asked me to do.

395
00:22:12,559 --> 00:22:14,200
The trial was postponed, wasn't it?

396
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:18,279
I handled the jurisdiction issue, right?

397
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:21,319
Why are you still haunting me?

398
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,000
What do you want?

399
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:25,319
Help me one last time.

400
00:22:26,279 --> 00:22:28,039
Do something you actually want to do.

401
00:22:30,119 --> 00:22:30,839
What is it?

402
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:32,640
Look, I drew this.

403
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:33,400
Let me see.

404
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:34,599
You drew this?

405
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,440
What did you draw here?

406
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,240
This is me.

407
00:22:38,359 --> 00:22:39,200
That's you?

408
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:39,960
And what about this?

409
00:22:40,759 --> 00:22:43,480
Grandpa and I taking a bath.

410
00:22:43,599 --> 00:22:44,400
This is Grandpa.

411
00:22:44,559 --> 00:22:45,160
Yeah.

412
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:46,960
Grandpa doesn't look this good.

413
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:47,640
Right?

414
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:50,319
This is the floor.

415
00:22:50,319 --> 00:22:52,920
Why doesn't the floor have any color?

416
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:54,200
Let's fill it in, okay?

417
00:22:54,559 --> 00:22:57,200
Look, that one is A'wu's too.

418
00:22:57,640 --> 00:22:58,680
A'wu is so talented!

419
00:22:58,759 --> 00:22:59,960
Yeah.

420
00:23:00,599 --> 00:23:02,119
He really likes drawing.

421
00:23:03,279 --> 00:23:04,160
Is that so, A'wu?

422
00:23:06,119 --> 00:23:08,240
What are you up to now?

423
00:23:08,839 --> 00:23:10,319
I know what you're thinking.

424
00:23:11,519 --> 00:23:13,960
You want to run away with your grandson.

425
00:23:14,039 --> 00:23:15,440
But you have to kill me first, right?

426
00:23:16,119 --> 00:23:18,279
Otherwise, no matter where you go,

427
00:23:18,599 --> 00:23:20,680
I will find you and tear you two apart.

428
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:23,839
So I'm giving you a chance.

429
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:27,640
The CFO of Fuxia Group...

430
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:29,359
has been missing for five days.

431
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:32,839
I bet Ma Tingting's team took him.

432
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,599
Fuxia Group might get sued again.

433
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,519
So before that happens, we need to

434
00:23:40,039 --> 00:23:42,119
plan a new fraudulent litigation scheme

435
00:23:42,599 --> 00:23:43,960
and secure asset preservation.

436
00:23:46,319 --> 00:23:47,599
Oh, I get it now.

437
00:23:50,799 --> 00:23:53,799
You just want me to help you get this done,

438
00:23:53,799 --> 00:23:55,240
then shift the blame to me.

439
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:58,440
I'll just be your scapegoat, right?

440
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,440
No, no, no, no.

441
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:02,880
Quite the opposite.

442
00:24:04,839 --> 00:24:06,519
If you help me with fraudulent litigation,

443
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:08,640
you'll finally be able to access

444
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:10,440
real evidence of my crimes.

445
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:14,680
That way, if you ever turn on me,

446
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:16,119
or decide not to cooperate anymore,

447
00:24:16,839 --> 00:24:19,240
you can destroy me anytime.

448
00:24:23,319 --> 00:24:26,000
Wouldn't not cooperating be safer?

449
00:24:27,599 --> 00:24:28,400
A'wu.

450
00:24:29,559 --> 00:24:30,599
Uncle is leaving now.

451
00:24:30,599 --> 00:24:31,799
Say good night to him.

452
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:34,880
Bye.

453
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:36,160
Don't say bye. Don't say bye.

454
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,119
You keep drawing, okay?

455
00:24:39,759 --> 00:24:41,079
Shouldn't you think about him?

456
00:24:44,680 --> 00:24:45,559
He is growing up.

457
00:24:46,599 --> 00:24:47,440
He needs to go to school.

458
00:24:48,559 --> 00:24:49,920
He needs a better life.

459
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:52,640
And think about yourself.

460
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:55,519
Before you get too sick,

461
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:58,559
shouldn't you save up more money for him?

462
00:25:00,799 --> 00:25:03,240
Even if you want to entrust him to Ding Ning

463
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:04,480
or anyone else,

464
00:25:06,079 --> 00:25:09,799
money is the most reliable guarantee.

465
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:17,880
What's wrong?

466
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:19,599
Have you seen Ding Ning lately?

467
00:25:22,279 --> 00:25:23,079
She...

468
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:25,880
has officially joined Rujie Law Firm.

469
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:30,200
She's been calling you non-stop every day.

470
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:32,880
But she definitely hasn't guessed

471
00:25:34,359 --> 00:25:36,480
that you threw your phone in the trash.

472
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:47,279
I'll tell you the truth.

473
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:48,920
The reason I approached you,

474
00:25:49,799 --> 00:25:51,279
and raised him all these years,

475
00:25:52,319 --> 00:25:53,799
was exactly for this.

476
00:25:56,759 --> 00:25:57,759
Help me out this time.

477
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,240
Name your price.

478
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:01,759
I absolutely won't bargain.

479
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:08,640
I want a deposit.

480
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:17,000
I'll give it to you when we get home.

481
00:26:21,839 --> 00:26:22,720
Are you done drawing?

482
00:26:23,119 --> 00:26:24,759
I added a little color down here.

483
00:26:24,759 --> 00:26:25,359
Where?

484
00:26:25,559 --> 00:26:25,880
Here.

485
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:26,440
Over here.

486
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:26,920
Right.

487
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:28,119
Let me help you color it, okay?

488
00:26:28,839 --> 00:26:30,160
Are you done drawing this tile?

489
00:26:31,240 --> 00:26:32,039
Halfway.

490
00:26:32,039 --> 00:26:32,799
Halfway.

491
00:26:33,119 --> 00:26:34,200
Then why aren't you drawing on this side?

492
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:37,240
Why aren't you drawing over here?

493
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,680
Let me help you draw it, okay?

494
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:54,960
You're back.

495
00:26:56,279 --> 00:26:57,799
What were you guys thinking?

496
00:26:58,400 --> 00:26:59,079
Look.

497
00:26:59,079 --> 00:27:00,599
Where have you been these past few days?

498
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:01,799
A'wu.

499
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:02,759
Ding Ning.

500
00:27:03,039 --> 00:27:04,079
Where did you and Grandpa go?

501
00:27:04,079 --> 00:27:05,319
Why didn't you even tell me?

502
00:27:05,319 --> 00:27:07,359
We just went on a trip for a few days.

503
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:09,720
You could've at least texted me.

504
00:27:09,720 --> 00:27:10,960
And you didn't answer my calls.

505
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:12,559
I just wanted some peace and quiet.

506
00:27:12,559 --> 00:27:13,640
I'm sorry.

507
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:14,559
Sorry about that.

508
00:27:14,559 --> 00:27:15,759
You still could've told me.

509
00:27:15,759 --> 00:27:17,200
My bad, my bad, my bad.

510
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:19,319
I'll let you know next time, okay?

511
00:27:19,319 --> 00:27:20,079
Seriously.

512
00:27:20,079 --> 00:27:21,000
You trust me that much?

513
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:22,599
Aren't you afraid I'd burn your house down?

514
00:27:23,400 --> 00:27:24,599
Not really, no.

515
00:27:25,079 --> 00:27:27,920
If you burn it down, where would you live?

516
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,240
I'm already looking for a place.

517
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:35,240
Who can handle being scared by you?

518
00:27:36,799 --> 00:27:38,160
Good, good.

519
00:27:38,839 --> 00:27:39,680
Move out then.

520
00:27:39,759 --> 00:27:41,359
That means you got a case.

521
00:27:41,480 --> 00:27:43,279
What is it? A big corporate case?

522
00:27:44,839 --> 00:27:47,119
I'd never get a big corporate case.

523
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:49,480
Just a small case no one else wants.

524
00:27:49,839 --> 00:27:51,279
That's fine. No one's fighting me for it.

525
00:27:51,759 --> 00:27:54,240
Actually, there are no small cases.

526
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:56,480
What kind of case is it?

527
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:57,359
Tell me about it.

528
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:01,920
The client in this case

529
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:04,160
is a 35-year-old programmer,

530
00:28:04,319 --> 00:28:05,119
Mr. Lin.

531
00:28:15,079 --> 00:28:16,039
On the day of the incident,

532
00:28:16,079 --> 00:28:17,519
Mr. Lin was having dinner with friends.

533
00:28:19,480 --> 00:28:20,640
He had driven there,

534
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:22,440
but was happy and had a few drinks.

535
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:23,839
Take it easy.

536
00:28:23,839 --> 00:28:24,640
Let's drink again next time.

537
00:28:30,119 --> 00:28:31,200
Didn't he call a designated driver?

538
00:28:31,759 --> 00:28:32,640
Did he want to save money,

539
00:28:33,559 --> 00:28:35,440
and just drive drunk?

540
00:28:36,640 --> 00:28:37,480
No.

541
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:40,079
He was afraid of waking his wife and kids,

542
00:28:40,079 --> 00:28:41,559
so he just slept in his car.

543
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:43,400
He planned to drive back after sobering up.

544
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,240
Hello, sir.

545
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:54,000
You're blocking traffic. Move forward a bit.

546
00:28:54,039 --> 00:28:54,839
Okay, I'll move it right away.

547
00:28:54,839 --> 00:28:55,680
A traffic cop told him

548
00:28:55,759 --> 00:28:57,400
he was parked in a no-parking zone

549
00:28:57,400 --> 00:28:58,359
and asked him to move his car.

550
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,799
So he moved it.

551
00:28:59,799 --> 00:29:01,640
He thought that since a night had passed,

552
00:29:01,759 --> 00:29:02,920
he was fine, right?

553
00:29:03,920 --> 00:29:05,200
So he drove the car

554
00:29:05,200 --> 00:29:06,759
to a parking spot a dozen meters away.

555
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:13,720
Hello, sir.

556
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:14,559
We're doing a breathalyzer test.

557
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:17,000
Hello, sir.

558
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:18,000
We're doing a breathalyzer test.

559
00:29:23,839 --> 00:29:24,640
Hello, sir.

560
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:25,519
We're doing a breathalyzer test.

561
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:37,680
First trial ruled it Dangerous Driving,

562
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:38,880
but exempted from criminal punishment.

563
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,920
This is our termination agreement.

564
00:29:47,200 --> 00:29:48,039
That's harsh.

565
00:29:48,759 --> 00:29:49,559
Terminated?

566
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:52,240
Can I record a video?

567
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:53,680
Sure, go ahead.

568
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:02,640
It's 11:30 PM.

569
00:30:04,160 --> 00:30:05,640
The head of HR is talking to me.

570
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:07,440
I'm recording this video as evidence.

571
00:30:08,599 --> 00:30:09,359
Please go ahead.

572
00:30:10,480 --> 00:30:11,599
Here's the thing, Lin.

573
00:30:11,960 --> 00:30:13,039
Regarding your work,

574
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:14,599
it's obvious to everyone.

575
00:30:14,599 --> 00:30:16,599
You're always dedicated and hardworking.

576
00:30:16,599 --> 00:30:17,359
You work overtime every day.

577
00:30:17,359 --> 00:30:18,640
And you never go home before midnight.

578
00:30:18,640 --> 00:30:20,079
Stop, stop. Just stop.

579
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,240
Can we talk about something real?

580
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:25,720
Zhang.

581
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:28,599
I've been working here since I graduated.

582
00:30:28,599 --> 00:30:29,920
Do you know how many years I've worked?

583
00:30:31,359 --> 00:30:32,400
Thirteen years.

584
00:30:33,319 --> 00:30:34,079
In your own words,

585
00:30:34,079 --> 00:30:35,119
I was dedicated.

586
00:30:35,119 --> 00:30:36,240
I was hardworking.

587
00:30:36,240 --> 00:30:37,440
Let's not even mention anything else.

588
00:30:38,119 --> 00:30:39,440
That year, the rival company

589
00:30:40,079 --> 00:30:42,119
offered me triple the salary

590
00:30:42,119 --> 00:30:42,839
to poach me.

591
00:30:42,839 --> 00:30:43,519
But I didn't leave.

592
00:30:43,519 --> 00:30:44,279
You know about this.

593
00:30:44,279 --> 00:30:44,720
Yes.

594
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:45,839
I really didn't leave!

595
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:46,759
What was I after?

596
00:30:46,759 --> 00:30:48,519
Wasn't it just my loyalty to our company?

597
00:30:48,519 --> 00:30:49,160
Wasn't it just because

598
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:50,359
I cared about our company?

599
00:30:50,519 --> 00:30:51,640
What do you mean by this now?

600
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:52,920
Do you think I'm too old now,

601
00:30:52,920 --> 00:30:54,279
and not as useful as the young ones?

602
00:30:54,279 --> 00:30:55,400
You're firing me just like that?

603
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:56,200
Is that what it is?

604
00:30:56,920 --> 00:30:58,079
Calm down, calm down.

605
00:30:58,720 --> 00:30:59,480
Lin.

606
00:31:00,319 --> 00:31:02,279
The company has clear rules. This labor...

607
00:31:02,279 --> 00:31:03,880
What rules are you talking about?

608
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:05,680
I was here before you even arrived!

609
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,359
Lecturing me about rules, Zhang Linsheng?

610
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:08,359
You're ridiculous.

611
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:11,319
We're both at this age.

612
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:12,599
We're middle-aged.

613
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,240
Firing me is one thing,

614
00:31:14,720 --> 00:31:16,680
but what about my wife and kid?

615
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:18,400
Who'll support our four elderly parents?

616
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:20,839
Who'll pay my mortgage and car loan?

617
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,559
I can't stop working for even a month!

618
00:31:22,759 --> 00:31:23,799
Help me figure this out.

619
00:31:23,799 --> 00:31:24,960
Calm down, calm down.

620
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:28,000
I completely understand what you're saying.

621
00:31:28,279 --> 00:31:29,559
But you know this,

622
00:31:30,039 --> 00:31:31,359
employees of Fuxia Group

623
00:31:31,359 --> 00:31:33,119
cannot have any criminal records.

624
00:31:33,759 --> 00:31:35,240
This is the company's red line.

625
00:31:37,039 --> 00:31:38,720
So even though I want to help you now,

626
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:40,440
my hands are tied.

627
00:31:43,759 --> 00:31:44,480
Sign it.

628
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:49,599
So, he was fined in the first trial.

629
00:31:49,599 --> 00:31:50,559
But he isn't satisfied with that,

630
00:31:50,559 --> 00:31:52,680
because it means his file...

631
00:31:52,680 --> 00:31:54,200
will have a criminal record.

632
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:57,119
He's afraid of getting fired.

633
00:31:57,119 --> 00:31:59,359
And finding a job later will be hard.

634
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:02,200
Mrs. Lin doesn't have a job,

635
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:04,359
and Mr. Lin is an only child.

636
00:32:04,640 --> 00:32:05,640
They have two kids,

637
00:32:05,640 --> 00:32:06,839
and four elderly parents at home.

638
00:32:06,839 --> 00:32:09,079
That means all eight people in his family...

639
00:32:09,079 --> 00:32:10,680
rely on his salary to survive.

640
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:12,839
So in the appeal trial, he wants to try...

641
00:32:12,839 --> 00:32:14,839
to get the charges dropped.

642
00:32:16,440 --> 00:32:17,640
Mrs. Lin said...

643
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:20,000
he'd even accept paying a heavier fine.

644
00:32:20,119 --> 00:32:21,720
But he just doesn't want to unjustly...

645
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:23,000
end up with a criminal record.

646
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:24,400
Only by protecting his innocence...

647
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:26,200
can they save their family's future.

648
00:32:26,279 --> 00:32:27,519
It's really not easy nowadays.

649
00:32:27,519 --> 00:32:28,319
The job market is bad,

650
00:32:28,319 --> 00:32:29,880
and at Mr. Lin's age,

651
00:32:29,880 --> 00:32:31,839
finding a job is even harder.

652
00:32:31,960 --> 00:32:33,000
It's the same for Mrs. Lin.

653
00:32:33,240 --> 00:32:34,039
You see, she's been at home...

654
00:32:34,039 --> 00:32:35,200
taking care of the kids for so long.

655
00:32:35,200 --> 00:32:36,480
Asking her to suddenly find a job...

656
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:37,519
wouldn't be easy either.

657
00:32:37,519 --> 00:32:38,359
As for the appeal trial,

658
00:32:39,359 --> 00:32:41,440
they usually don't hold a hearing.

659
00:32:41,519 --> 00:32:43,680
Securing an appeal trial hearing is key.

660
00:32:44,599 --> 00:32:45,400
I know.

661
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:46,920
But the law firm still hasn't...

662
00:32:46,920 --> 00:32:48,200
given me the authorization yet.

663
00:32:48,799 --> 00:32:49,480
Why?

664
00:32:49,519 --> 00:32:50,519
Why won't they issue it?

665
00:32:50,519 --> 00:32:51,599
Do they not want you to take the case?

666
00:32:53,119 --> 00:32:54,680
It's fine. It'll get sorted out.

667
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:58,920
Can you do me a favor tomorrow?

668
00:32:59,839 --> 00:33:00,839
Shoot. What is it?

669
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:02,599
You know I'm apartment hunting.

670
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:03,799
The agent sent me a few options,

671
00:33:03,799 --> 00:33:05,319
and I booked viewings for tomorrow noon.

672
00:33:05,519 --> 00:33:07,839
But Mrs. Lin wants to meet about the case.

673
00:33:07,839 --> 00:33:08,440
So...

674
00:33:08,599 --> 00:33:09,839
Then I'll go see them for you.

675
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:11,519
No problem.

676
00:33:13,359 --> 00:33:14,759
They're not far. Just nearby.

677
00:33:14,759 --> 00:33:15,400
Okay then.

678
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:16,960
Just give me the agent's number.

679
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:19,200
Alright.

680
00:33:25,079 --> 00:33:26,519
Living close by has its perks.

681
00:33:27,119 --> 00:33:28,000
Don't worry.

682
00:33:28,119 --> 00:33:29,519
I'll come over for free meals often.

683
00:33:42,640 --> 00:33:43,440
Watch your step.

684
00:33:44,400 --> 00:33:46,440
Older buildings just have a lot of stairs.

685
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:48,680
But it's a quiet spot in a busy area.

686
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:49,960
It's great value for money.

687
00:33:50,279 --> 00:33:51,359
I wonder what Mr. Yu

688
00:33:51,519 --> 00:33:52,720
thinks of this apartment.

689
00:33:53,559 --> 00:33:54,319
Tell you what.

690
00:33:54,319 --> 00:33:57,160
I think I'd still like to look around

691
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:58,799
to find one with a better orientation.

692
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:00,960
One that gets a bit more sunlight.

693
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:02,000
Where's my jaw harp?

694
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,039
And look over here.

695
00:34:03,359 --> 00:34:04,279
There are a lot of cars.

696
00:34:05,039 --> 00:34:06,559
Going back and forth, it'll be noisy.

697
00:34:09,519 --> 00:34:10,840
Where did I drop it?

698
00:34:12,639 --> 00:34:14,079
Where's my jaw harp?

699
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:24,920
My jaw harp.

700
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:25,679
Give it back to me.

701
00:34:26,199 --> 00:34:27,159
Just come inside first.

702
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:39,400
Your house?

703
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:40,159
What do you think?

704
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:50,159
I'm not a thief.

705
00:34:51,559 --> 00:34:52,800
I just came back to look around.

706
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:56,360
When this house was just a concrete shell,

707
00:34:56,800 --> 00:34:57,760
I'd already seen it.

708
00:34:59,599 --> 00:35:00,599
To tell you the truth,

709
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:02,920
my dad built this house.

710
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:09,119
This...

711
00:35:10,239 --> 00:35:11,199
That's a trampoline.

712
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:32,800
I wanted to know what kind of people

713
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,079
live in the house my dad built.

714
00:35:34,079 --> 00:35:35,119
What's your name?

715
00:35:35,280 --> 00:35:37,079
Yang A'wu. And you?

716
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,599
Just call me Xiao Lu.

717
00:35:40,880 --> 00:35:41,760
You live around here?

718
00:35:47,840 --> 00:35:48,599
Right here.

719
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:50,440
Grandpa's afraid I'll get lost.

720
00:35:50,599 --> 00:35:51,679
So many words.

721
00:35:52,199 --> 00:35:53,280
Can you read them all?

722
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:55,360
I'm older than you.

723
00:35:55,360 --> 00:35:56,519
How could I not?

724
00:35:57,480 --> 00:35:58,320
How old are you?

725
00:35:58,719 --> 00:35:59,920
I'm eight.

726
00:36:00,079 --> 00:36:01,480
I'm thirteen. Call me brother.

727
00:36:07,519 --> 00:36:08,400
How do you play this?

728
00:36:32,199 --> 00:36:32,880
Sure.

729
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:35,800
The price might be a bit high.

730
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:37,000
I don't know what you think.

731
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:38,840
Where's the kid?

732
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:40,000
The kid? He went upstairs.

733
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:41,079
He ran up there.

734
00:36:41,159 --> 00:36:41,960
A'wu!

735
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:43,760
A'wu!

736
00:36:45,039 --> 00:36:45,760
A'wu!

737
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:48,119
Your folks are calling you.

738
00:36:48,119 --> 00:36:50,039
Let's go. Don't let him see us.

739
00:36:51,360 --> 00:36:52,440
You forgot this.

740
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:55,159
Keep it.

741
00:37:08,440 --> 00:37:09,480
What were you doing?

742
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:12,519
Why not tell Grandpa before running off?

743
00:37:12,639 --> 00:37:14,440
What if I couldn't find you?

744
00:37:17,440 --> 00:37:19,280
Mr. Yu, we'll take you to take a look.

745
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:19,880
Excuse me.

746
00:37:20,639 --> 00:37:21,719
Hello? What is it?

747
00:37:22,159 --> 00:37:23,079
Yang Cheng is dead.

748
00:37:27,719 --> 00:37:28,360
Okay.

749
00:37:30,599 --> 00:37:31,239
Okay.

750
00:37:43,519 --> 00:37:44,719
Some other time. I'll call you.

751
00:37:44,719 --> 00:37:45,440
Today

752
00:37:46,800 --> 00:37:47,840
That's enough for today.

753
00:37:48,320 --> 00:37:49,000
Sorry about that.

754
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,280
No worries. Take care.

755
00:38:03,119 --> 00:38:04,719
There's no photo of the old man.

756
00:38:04,719 --> 00:38:06,599
Not even a portrait on the urn.

757
00:38:09,039 --> 00:38:11,719
Did you find Liang Zidong?

758
00:38:11,800 --> 00:38:12,639
No.

759
00:38:13,519 --> 00:38:14,119
I've mobilized

760
00:38:14,119 --> 00:38:16,239
all the firm's experienced criminal lawyers.

761
00:38:16,559 --> 00:38:17,880
But there's been no progress.

762
00:38:17,880 --> 00:38:19,079
Is it that hard?

763
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:22,079
With the police and prosecutors on guard,

764
00:38:22,079 --> 00:38:23,199
yes, it is that hard.

765
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:26,159
Luckily, I kept a trick up my sleeve.

766
00:38:26,679 --> 00:38:28,079
And I still have you in the shadows.

767
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:29,320
Don't give me that.

768
00:38:30,159 --> 00:38:31,320
I've already agreed to help you

769
00:38:31,320 --> 00:38:33,199
deal with the fraudulent litigation base.

770
00:38:33,320 --> 00:38:35,800
You handle the rest yourself, okay?

771
00:38:39,079 --> 00:38:40,920
This... how should we handle this?

772
00:38:41,880 --> 00:38:43,719
I see a line for cemetery plots over there.

773
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:45,039
Leave it at the depository.

774
00:38:45,039 --> 00:38:45,840
I get it now.

775
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:47,559
I'll handle it myself.

776
00:38:47,559 --> 00:38:48,199
It's not your place.

777
00:38:48,199 --> 00:38:49,559
You're not related to him.

778
00:38:50,199 --> 00:38:53,000
Enshrining the man who killed your family...

779
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:54,079
that's just weird.

780
00:38:54,079 --> 00:38:56,079
Can you watch your mouth?

781
00:38:56,840 --> 00:38:57,840
Well, then what should we do?

782
00:38:58,280 --> 00:38:59,280
Keep it at your place?

783
00:38:59,599 --> 00:39:00,760
What if you scatter his ashes one day,

784
00:39:01,239 --> 00:39:02,480
and his family comes looking?

785
00:39:03,039 --> 00:39:05,239
You have news of his daughter, right?

786
00:39:06,239 --> 00:39:08,320
I'm just saying what if... what if.

787
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:11,159
Why are you so nervous?

788
00:39:11,840 --> 00:39:13,199
Then tell me what to do with it.

789
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:18,519
How about keeping it at my place for now?

790
00:39:20,159 --> 00:39:20,960
Sorry for the trouble.

791
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:22,039
Also,

792
00:39:22,199 --> 00:39:24,760
don't tell A'wu about Yang Cheng yet, okay?

793
00:39:25,079 --> 00:39:25,760
Please.

794
00:39:30,559 --> 00:39:31,159
Okay.

795
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,840
I know how to find Liang Zidong.

796
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:49,840
Are you in?
